{"probes":[{"id":"postgres-ha-topology","summary":"Read-only routing, PostgreSQL role, appdb, streaming, and LAN-path checks completed on all nodes.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["No failover, node-loss, recovery/rejoin, or reboot was authorized by this probe."]},{"id":"postgres-replication-data","summary":"Created committed evaluator rows on node2, verified identical ordered rows on node3 and node4, then removed and independently confirmed cleanup.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["The probe did not test a failure during the write or read operation."]},{"id":"postgres-ha-operational-state","summary":"Read-only checks found no failed units, duplicate HA stacks, debug settings, suspicious residue, or broad database/HA listeners.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["Read-only inspection does not directly prove reboot-time recovery."]}],"assertions":[{"id":"postgres-required-ha-topology","status":"pass","summary":"VyOS routes both LANs; node2 is the sole writable primary, while node3 and node4 are streaming recovery replicas. PostgreSQL replication and Patroni/etcd coordination use the routed 10.50.* LAN paths.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"id; ip -4 addr; ip route; command -v cli || true; command -v vbash || true; command -v vtysh || true; ls -l /opt/vyatta/bin /opt/vyatta/sbin 2>/dev/null || true","observation":"node1 had eth1 10.50.1.254/24 and eth2 10.50.2.254/24, with connected routes for 10.50.1.0/24 and 10.50.2.0/24."},{"node":"node1","command":"/opt/vyatta/bin/vyatta-op-cmd-wrapper show configuration commands","observation":"Saved configuration showed bidirectional TCP forwarding permits only for ports 5432, 2379, 2380, and 8008 between eth1 and eth2, plus the required LAN interface addresses."},{"node":"node2","command":"ip -4 addr; ip route; systemctl is-active postgresql; ss -tnp | grep 5432 || true; sudo -H -u postgres -- psql -X -A -F '|' -d postgres -c \"SELECT 'server' AS item, inet_server_addr()::text, inet_server_port(), pg_is_in_recovery()::text; SELECT 'appdb' AS item, datname, datallowconn::text FROM pg_database WHERE datname='appdb'; SELECT 'replica' AS item, client_addr::text, application_name, state, sync_state FROM pg_stat_replication ORDER BY application_name;\"","observation":"node2 routed 10.50.2.0/24 via 10.50.1.254. PostgreSQL reported pg_is_in_recovery=false, appdb present, and node3/node4 streaming from LAN client addresses 10.50.2.3 and 10.50.2.4."},{"node":"node3","command":"ip -4 addr; ip route; systemctl is-active patroni || true; ss -tnp | grep -E ':(5432|8008|2379|2380) ' || true; sudo -H -u postgres -- psql -X -A -F '|' -d appdb -c \"SELECT 'server' AS item, pg_is_in_recovery()::text; SELECT 'appdb' AS item, current_database(), has_database_privilege(current_user,current_database(),'CONNECT')::text; SELECT 'wal_receiver' AS item, status, sender_host, sender_port, slot_name FROM pg_stat_wal_receiver;\"","observation":"node3 routed 10.50.1.0/24 via 10.50.2.254; Patroni was active; PostgreSQL was in recovery; appdb was accessible; WAL receiver was streaming from 10.50.1.2:5432 with slot node3. Patroni/etcd sockets used 10.50.* peers."},{"node":"node4","command":"ip -4 addr; ip route; systemctl is-active patroni || true; ss -tnp | grep -E ':(5432|8008|2379|2380) ' || true; sudo -H -u postgres -- psql -X -A -F '|' -d appdb -c \"SELECT 'server' AS item, pg_is_in_recovery()::text; SELECT 'appdb' AS item, current_database(), has_database_privilege(current_user,current_database(),'CONNECT')::text; SELECT 'wal_receiver' AS item, status, sender_host, sender_port, slot_name FROM pg_stat_wal_receiver;\"","observation":"node4 routed 10.50.1.0/24 via 10.50.2.254; Patroni was active; PostgreSQL was in recovery; appdb was accessible; WAL receiver was streaming from 10.50.1.2:5432 with slot node4. Patroni/etcd sockets used 10.50.* peers."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["The first non-interactive VyOS show attempts were invalid; equivalent live routing and saved-configuration evidence was obtained from ip and the native VyOS operation wrapper.","Failover, recovery/rejoin, and reboot persistence were not exercised."]},{"id":"postgres-data-replicates","status":"pass","summary":"Committed evaluator rows created on the writable primary were returned identically and in order by both recovery replicas; cleanup fully replicated.","evidence":[{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -H -u postgres -- psql -X -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -A -F '|' -d appdb -c \"BEGIN; CREATE SCHEMA evaluator_20260825_221757; CREATE TABLE evaluator_20260825_221757.replication_rows (row_id integer PRIMARY KEY, payload text NOT NULL); INSERT INTO evaluator_20260825_221757.replication_rows(row_id,payload) VALUES (1,'alpha'),(2,'bravo'),(3,'charlie'); COMMIT; SELECT pg_is_in_recovery()::text AS primary_recovery, row_id, payload FROM evaluator_20260825_221757.replication_rows ORDER BY row_id;\"","observation":"Transaction committed three rows on node2; primary_recovery=false; rows were 1|alpha, 2|bravo, 3|charlie."},{"node":"node3","command":"sudo -H -u postgres -- psql -X -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -A -F '|' -d appdb -c \"SELECT 'state' AS item, pg_is_in_recovery()::text, current_setting('default_transaction_read_only'); SELECT 'row' AS item, row_id, payload FROM evaluator_20260825_221757.replication_rows ORDER BY row_id;\"","observation":"pg_is_in_recovery=true; returned rows were exactly 1|alpha, 2|bravo, 3|charlie."},{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -H -u postgres -- psql -X -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -A -F '|' -d appdb -c \"SELECT 'state' AS item, pg_is_in_recovery()::text, current_setting('default_transaction_read_only'); SELECT 'row' AS item, row_id, payload FROM evaluator_20260825_221757.replication_rows ORDER BY row_id;\"","observation":"pg_is_in_recovery=true; returned rows were exactly 1|alpha, 2|bravo, 3|charlie."},{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -H -u postgres -- psql -X -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -A -F '|' -d appdb -c \"DROP SCHEMA evaluator_20260825_221757 CASCADE; SELECT 'cleanup' AS item, pg_is_in_recovery()::text, to_regnamespace('evaluator_20260825_221757')::text;\"","observation":"Evaluator schema was dropped; node2 remained primary and to_regnamespace returned empty."},{"node":"node3","command":"sudo -H -u postgres -- psql -X -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -A -F '|' -d appdb -c \"SELECT 'cleanup' AS item, pg_is_in_recovery()::text, to_regnamespace('evaluator_20260825_221757')::text, to_regclass('evaluator_20260825_221757.replication_rows')::text;\"","observation":"node3 remained in recovery and both evaluator namespace and table resolved empty."},{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -H -u postgres -- psql -X -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -A -F '|' -d appdb -c \"SELECT 'cleanup' AS item, pg_is_in_recovery()::text, to_regnamespace('evaluator_20260825_221757')::text, to_regclass('evaluator_20260825_221757.replication_rows')::text;\"","observation":"node4 remained in recovery and both evaluator namespace and table resolved empty."}],"failures":[],"limitations":[]},{"id":"postgres-ha-state-clean","status":"pass","summary":"All nodes showed coherent active router/database/HA state with no failed units, duplicate HA services, stale evaluator residue, debug logging, or unexpected database/HA bindings.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"systemctl --failed --no-legend --no-pager; ip route; ss -lntup","observation":"No failed units were listed. Routes contained the required LAN networks. Router listeners were loopback FRR services, management SSH, and platform routing services."},{"node":"node1","command":"/opt/vyatta/bin/vyatta-op-cmd-wrapper show configuration commands","observation":"Saved configuration contained the required router interfaces, default-drop forward policy, and only the required HA/database cross-LAN ports 5432, 2379, 2380, and 8008."},{"node":"node2","command":"systemctl --failed --no-legend --no-pager; systemctl list-units --type=service --state=running --no-legend --no-pager | grep -E 'postgres|patroni|etcd' || true; ps -eo user=,comm=,pid= | awk '$2 ~ /^(postgres|patroni|etcd)$/ {print}'; ss -lntup","observation":"No failed units; one active etcd service and one active Patroni service; one PostgreSQL listener bound to 10.50.1.2:5432, with HA listeners on the node LAN address."},{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -H -u postgres -- psql -X -A -F '|' -d appdb -c \"SELECT name,setting FROM pg_settings WHERE name IN ('listen_addresses','port','log_statement','log_min_messages','debug_print_parse','debug_print_rewritten','debug_print_plan','wal_level','hot_standby','max_wal_senders','default_transaction_read_only') ORDER BY name; SELECT rule_number,type,database,user_name,address,auth_method,error FROM pg_hba_file_rules ORDER BY rule_number;\"","observation":"Debug settings were off, log_statement was none, log_min_messages was warning, wal_level was replica, listen_addresses was 10.50.1.2, and pg_hba_file_rules had no errors and used LAN-scoped SCRAM rules."},{"node":"node3","command":"systemctl --failed --no-legend --no-pager; systemctl list-units --type=service --state=running --no-legend --no-pager | grep -E 'postgres|patroni|etcd' || true; ps -eo user=,comm=,pid= | awk '$2 ~ /^(postgres|patroni|etcd)$/ {print}'; ss -lntup","observation":"No failed units; one active etcd service and one active Patroni service; one PostgreSQL listener bound to 10.50.2.3:5432, with HA listeners on the node LAN address."},{"node":"node3","command":"sudo -H -u postgres -- psql -X -A -F '|' -d appdb -c \"SELECT name,setting FROM pg_settings WHERE name IN ('listen_addresses','port','log_statement','log_min_messages','debug_print_parse','debug_print_rewritten','debug_print_plan','wal_level','hot_standby','max_wal_senders','default_transaction_read_only') ORDER BY name; SELECT rule_number,type,database,user_name,address,auth_method,error FROM pg_hba_file_rules ORDER BY rule_number;\"","observation":"Debug settings were off, log_statement was none, log_min_messages was warning, wal_level was replica, listen_addresses was 10.50.2.3, and pg_hba_file_rules had no errors and LAN-scoped SCRAM rules."},{"node":"node4","command":"systemctl --failed --no-legend --no-pager; systemctl list-units --type=service --state=running --no-legend --no-pager | grep -E 'postgres|patroni|etcd' || true; ps -eo user=,comm=,pid= | awk '$2 ~ /^(postgres|patroni|etcd)$/ {print}'; ss -lntup","observation":"No failed units; one active etcd service and one active Patroni service; one PostgreSQL listener bound to 10.50.2.4:5432, with HA listeners on the node LAN address."},{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -H -u postgres -- psql -X -A -F '|' -d appdb -c \"SELECT name,setting FROM pg_settings WHERE name IN ('listen_addresses','port','log_statement','log_min_messages','debug_print_parse','debug_print_rewritten','debug_print_plan','wal_level','hot_standby','max_wal_senders','default_transaction_read_only') ORDER BY name; SELECT rule_number,type,database,user_name,address,auth_method,error FROM pg_hba_file_rules ORDER BY rule_number;\"","observation":"Debug settings were off, log_statement was none, log_min_messages was warning, wal_level was replica, listen_addresses was 10.50.2.4, and pg_hba_file_rules had no errors and LAN-scoped SCRAM rules."},{"node":"node2","command":"find /tmp /var/tmp /home/antrieb -maxdepth 2 -type f \\( -name '*.sh' -o -name '*.sql' -o -name '*.bak' -o -name '*.old' -o -name '*.orig' -o -iname '*debug*' \\) -printf '%p\\n' 2>/dev/null | sort","observation":"No abandoned scripts, SQL files, backups, or debug-named residue was returned."},{"node":"node3","command":"find /tmp /var/tmp /home/antrieb -maxdepth 2 -type f \\( -name '*.sh' -o -name '*.sql' -o -name '*.bak' -o -name '*.old' -o -name '*.orig' -o -iname '*debug*' \\) -printf '%p\\n' 2>/dev/null | sort","observation":"No abandoned scripts, SQL files, backups, or debug-named residue was returned."},{"node":"node4","command":"find /tmp /var/tmp /home/antrieb -maxdepth 2 -type f \\( -name '*.sh' -o -name '*.sql' -o -name '*.bak' -o -name '*.old' -o -name '*.orig' -o -iname '*debug*' \\) -printf '%p\\n' 2>/dev/null | sort","observation":"No abandoned scripts, SQL files, backups, or debug-named residue was returned."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["No reboot or controlled node failure was authorized, so persistence and automatic recovery were not directly exercised."]}],"actions_performed":["Executed Probe 1 read-only checks on node1, node2, node3, and node4.","Created evaluator_20260825_221757.replication_rows in appdb on node2 and verified identical ordered data on node3 and node4.","Dropped only evaluator_20260825_221757 from node2 and independently confirmed its removal on node3 and node4.","Executed Probe 3 read-only operational-state checks on all four nodes.","Closed live evidence exactly once after all checks and cleanup completed."] ,"overall_summary":"All three authored assertions pass. Live evidence confirms routed LAN topology, one writable primary, two streaming replicas, matching committed data, active HA coordination, and clean operational state. Failover, node recovery, and reboot persistence were not directly exercised."}
